REJECTED -- DO NOT APPLY. Validated on cuttlefish riscv64: this patch MAKES THE LEAK WORSE.
eglReleaseThread() drops the thread's HostConnection, but the host never reclaims it because
EGL ownership is keyed by the virtio process-pipe counter while cleanup is keyed by the ctx id
(virtio_gpu_pipe.cpp -> HostConnection.cpp -> render_control.cpp vs virtio_gpu_context.cpp).
So each release-and-recreate strands another set. The acquisition site identified below is
still correct; the release mechanism is not. The fix belongs in the host (gfxstream) keying,
plus the single-GL-thread change in 0002. Kept for the record.
